    if whole == 0:
        if part == 0:
            return float("nan")
        return float("inf")
    return float(part) / float(whole) * 100

def test():
    a = [1, 2, 3, -1, -3, -2]
    total = sum(a)
    return percentage(sum(a[:-3]), total)

print(test())
```

This code will help you understand the values being processed and ensure that any potential division by zero is handled properly.

